# Copy to .env.local for local development. Vercel holds the deployed values.

# Origin of the Insights app, which owns the WorkOS handoff. Every Sign in /
# Sign up control on this site points at `<origin>/api/auth/sign-in` and
# `/api/auth/sign-up`, and the plan cards hand it a `next` of `/upgrade?...`.
#
# It is also where the PRICES come from. `next build` fetches
# `<origin>/api/public/plans` once and the pricing cards render from it, so this
# variable decides which deployment of Insights the advertised prices belong to.
# That endpoint is unauthenticated and must be reachable from the build; if it
# is not, the build prints a loud PLANS warning and falls back to the static
# mirror in `lib/plans.ts` rather than failing. See `lib/insights-plans.ts`.
#
# Optional. Unset or blank falls back to the production origin below, which is
# what a production build wants; set it to point a preview build of this funnel
# at a preview deployment of Insights.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means BUILD TIME. The value is inlined into the bundle when
# `next build` runs, so changing it in the Vercel dashboard does nothing on its
# own -- the project has to be redeployed for the new value to take effect.
#
# No trailing slash needed; one is stripped either way.
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSIGHTS_URL=https://insights.bulkloads.com

# GA4 Measurement ID. When set, `app/layout.tsx` mounts `<GoogleAnalytics>` from
# `@next/third-parties`; when unset or blank, no analytics load at all.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means BUILD TIME (see above): the ID is inlined at `next build`,
# so a value added in Vercel does nothing until the project is redeployed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# Meta pixel id, in the form of a long number. Optional: the id is defaulted in
# components/MetaPixel.tsx, because a pixel id is public and ships in the
# page's HTML anyway, so a correct production build needs nothing set here.
#
# Set it to point a deployment at a DIFFERENT pixel, or set it locally to a
# throwaway id to test the wiring: the pixel is off in development unless this
# is set, so that a developer's clicks never land in the ad account that is
# optimising live campaigns.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
